# ~/.autopilot/endpoints.env — autopilot heterogeneous-engine credentials (mode 600).
# Copy to ~/.autopilot/endpoints.env (or run `scripts/load-endpoints-env.sh --init`), chmod 600.
# ONE canonical home for Anthropic-compatible endpoint tokens (GLM / MiniMax / any compatible).
# NEVER commit the filled-in copy. Parsed SAFELY (not sourced): only `NAME=VALUE` lines with an
# allowlisted NAME are honored; a set env var always wins. Uncomment + fill what you use.
#
# Prefer a SUBSCRIPTION / coding-plan token over a metered API key. OAuth-login runners
# (codex / agy / grok) need NOTHING here — they use their own CLI login.
#
# Convention: AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_<NAME>_URL + _TOKEN  (<NAME> is [A-Za-z0-9_], your own label).
#
# --- GLM (Zhipu) coding plan ---
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_GLM_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_GLM_TOKEN=
#
# --- MiniMax (intl) ---
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_MINIMAX_URL=https://api.minimax.io/anthropic
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_MINIMAX_TOKEN=
#
# --- A local model on YOUR OWN LAN (SGLang / vLLM / llama.cpp serving /v1/messages) ---
# Default policy is https:// or loopback http://. For a private-range IP LITERAL only
# (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 169.254/16, fc00::/7, fe80::/10 — never a hostname), the
# explicit opt-in below permits plaintext http://. It is DISCLOSED everywhere (list/which/
# doctor, resolve-endpoint transport_security, a notice on every dispatch) and it does not
# encrypt anything: bearer + prompts (repo contents) cross the LAN in the clear. Shared
# server → put TLS + an api-key in front of it and drop the _TRANSPORT line instead.
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_QWEN38_URL=http://192.168.101.7:8001
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_QWEN38_TOKEN=local-no-auth
# AUTOPILOT_ENDPOINT_QWEN38_TRANSPORT=plaintext-private
